this video was made possible thanks to  our friends over at class  - central.com / Pakman click the link  under this video to browse tens of  thousands of college lectures from the  world's top universities let's talk  about telekinesis also known as psycho  Kinesis it's the ability to influence  physical matter supernaturally with the  mind someone who claims to have  telekinesis claims that they can move or  physically manipulate objects without  physically interacting with that object  so examples can include making an object  levitate transmuting an object into  another object supernaturally affecting  someone's biology such as healing  someone with a disease for example  telekinesis can be thought of as a type  of psychic power but a distinction is  sometimes made between a psychic and a  telekinetic psychics are considered to  be people who know things through  supernatural means telekinetics are  people who can physically move or change  things a person who is knowingly  creating the illusion of manipulating  objects but doesn't claim to have  supernatural powers would call  themselves a magician for example or an  illusionist in this case it's more of a  performance-art but someone who truly  believes that they're able to move  objects with their mind or is trying to  deceive their audience into believing as  much will assert that they're really  telekinetic in the famous Hindu myth  called ma bharata written around 400 BC  one of the two major Sanskrit epics of  ancient India the stories plot centers  around the character Shakuni and his  manipulation of dice to influence a game  in his favor this might be the first  instance of telekinesis known in fiction  then of course there's Jesus who might  be the most famous telekinetic of all  time turning water into wine curing  people of blindness feeding 5,000 people  with five loaves of bread and two fish  according to the New Testament of course  there was the wizard Merlin from The  Legend of King Arthur in the 12th  century who through telekinetic powers  across the ocean in a glass house and  built Stonehenge according to the tale  even though telekinesis has been a theme  in fiction and mythology for centuries  it didn't really gained much popularity  as something actually done in front of  an audience until the 19th century the  term telekinesis was first coined by  Russian writer Alexander axe akov during  his fascination with a British woman  known as Madame desperat Suh performed  seances through Europe tricking people  into believing that she could do things  like talking to the dead using her mind  to move tables making flowers appear out  of thin air acts akov was a journalist  and researcher of supernatural phenomena  and after spending time with DES piron's  praised her wrote about her as a real  honest telekinetic despero's was later  proven to be a fraud beginning in 1880  during a performance where an audience  member actually caught her pretending to  be a ghost few years later during a  performance where she claimed to  dematerialize the lower half of her body  an audience member again caught her  squeezing her legs through the back of  her chair Despero is the first person  described with the word telekinetic is  probably the most famous fraudulent  telekinetic of late 1800s another study  subject of Alexander axe akov was an  Italian woman named you say Pia  Palladino Palladino put on shows murk  making her audience believes she was  able to talk to the dead and levitate  objects the British Society for  psychical research caught Paladino on  multiple occasions just using simple  tricks to create the illusion she  claimed were telekinetic phenomena she  used sleight of hand techniques she used  her foot to move furniture she claimed  to be moving with her mind she even tied  long strands of hair on objects to make  them appear to float in the air world  renowned illusionist Harry Houdini wrote  a book in 1920 called miracle mongers  and their methods and he exposed frauds  like desperat Zinn Palladino the book  actually chronicled the history of fake  telekinetics and gives detailed  explanations of how they created these  illusions there's been widespread  scientific consensus since  the 1800s that telekinesis is pure  pseudoscience in 1988 the National  Research Council in the u.s. actually  commissioned a panel to research this  they reviewed a hundred and thirty years  of past scientific research on  telekinesis and they said in their  conclusion quote evaluation of a large  body of the best available evidence  simply does not support the contention  that these phenomena exists around the  same time the US Army and the National  Academy of Sciences formed a panel to  study the evidence for telekinesis and  to assess whether it might have military  and intelligence applications for  example they wanted to figure out could  individuals use telekinesis to remotely  sabotage enemy weaponry you can be sure  that if there was any validity to  telekinesis the US military would do  everything possible to discover and make  use of it but they had no such luck the  panel was completely unable to find any  scientific evidence to support the  existence of telekinesis so ask yourself  what's more likely that people have been  convinced of telekinesis only through  trickery and faulty experimental design  or that the fields of neuroscience and  physics need to be completely reinvented  to account for telekinesis through  physics we know how matter behaves and  why Caltech physicist Sean Carroll has  written about telekinesis and has  pointed out that all of the objects  telekinetics claimed to bend or levitate  consist of atoms and that any movement  of these atoms would require telekinesis  to use means other than the four known  fundamental forces of nature those were  the strong nuclear force the weak  nuclear force electromagnetism and  gravitation Carroll said that if  telekinesis uses a new undiscovered  fifth fourth of nature simple math shows  that it would need to be about 1 billion  the strength of gravity has to go  undetected by all other prior physics  research and gravity is simply not  strong enough to bend a spoon Carroll  says quote and that's it we are done the  deep lesson is that although science  doesn't know everything  it's not anything goes either there are  well defined regimes of physical  phenomena where we do know how things  work . the place to look for new and  surprising phenomena is outside those  regimes you don't need to set up  elaborate double-blind protocols to pass  judgment on the abilities of purported  psychics British physicist John Taylor  was originally a believer in telekinesis  he was inspired by the supposed  telekinetic uri geller  who's famous for bending metal spoons  and taylor spent four years conducting  research on possible causes of  telekinesis by the end of his long  in-depth exploration Taylor concluded  there's no plausible physical mechanism  for telekinesis Taylor said that all of  the supposed telekinesis he studied  ended up having other naturalistic  explanations and that no actual  telekinesis occurred under  scientifically controlled conditions uri  geller who I mentioned is probably the  most famous purported telekinetic of all  time he's been making TV appearances and  performing for live audiences since the  late 1960s and his career has turned him  into a multimillionaire he's claimed to  have telepathic and telekinetic powers  given to him by aliens his most well  known routine is to bend metal spoons  which he says he does with his mind but  Geller spoon bending has been  demonstrated time and time again by  magicians to be completely possible  through simple magic tricks and illusion  in the early 70s Geller was successfully  sued for fraud and was court ordered to  refund the ticket price to the man who  sued him Geller only agrees to bend  spoons in certain situations he was  enabled to bend any spoons when he  appeared on The Tonight Show with Johnny  Carson in 1973 Nobel prize-winning  physicist Richard Fineman has said that  Geller was unable to perform the trick  on demand when they met in person and as  of 2007 Geller has more or less admitted  that he doesn't actually have  supernatural powers science has long  been eager to find real evidence of  telekinesis  but telekinesis has always managed to  come up short from 1964 to 2015 there  was even a legitimate million dollar  prize offered by the  James Randi Educational Foundation which  we've spoken about before to anyone who  could demonstrate telekinetic or other  supernatural abilities and no one was  ever successful in collecting that  million dollars and still to this day no  scientists have been able to properly  replicate claims about telekinesis in  controlled lab conditions of course it's  true that scientific research has the  ability to completely overturn what we  think we know scientifically it is  possible that someday we'll be able to  prove the existence of telekinesis but  tests must be conducted under the most  stringent conditions to reverse a  century of established science people  claiming telekinetic powers and people  who believe in telekinesis need to  understand why strict standards must be  applied to experiments that examine the  supposed phenomenon it's because  telekinesis would defy facts that are  firmly settled in physics and  neurobiology that we need those strict  conditions and until now it's not  something that telekinesis has been able  to live up to period if you want to  learn more about the scientific method  and why certain types of claims require  specific types of scientific evidence  click the link under this video and  check out the great new course offered  by the University of Edinburgh called  introduction to the philosophy of  physical sciences it's one of thousands  of courses you'll find at class -  central.com / Pakman whether it's  political science psychology sociology  physics business comps I almost anything  you can imagine they have courses from  MIT Stanford Berkeley and tons of the  courses are totally free get started  watching College lectures on topics you  love right now by clicking the link  underneath this video
 

